      "value": "@{5ab3ad272b67505f726c2a8f|full_name}: I am uploading my world as a new build. I did finally find what you were talking about. I've never accessed this location for unity stuff. Okay, so basically what's taking up the most space is \"file headers\" at a whopping 71.5% and surprisingly I don't think I see any unused assets in the list. The full percentages for the uncompressed usage is this:\n\nTextures               87.4 mb\t 16.0% \nMeshes                 7.5 mb\t 1.4% \nAnimations             0.0 kb\t 0.0% \nSounds                 2.3 mb\t 0.4% \nShaders                12.9 mb\t 2.4% \nOther Assets           1.4 mb\t 0.3% \nLevels                 44.0 mb\t 8.1% \nScripts                1.9 kb\t 0.0% \nIncluded DLLs          0.0 kb\t 0.0% \nFile headers           390.4 mb\t 71.5% \nTotal User Assets      545.9 mb\t 100.0% \nComplete build size    545.9 mb\n\nI have no idea if I have any control over the file headers section. I do know I have control over the textures, however I've already been compressing them as much as possible without lowering their quality. I still find it weird that I updated the sdk and *removed* stuff from the world only to have the file size increase.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
